        "title": "Keep legacy WhatsApp crontab lint opt-in",
        "body": "## Summary\n- mark `core/doctor/legacy-whatsapp-crontab` default-disabled so default `doctor --lint` does not invoke the `crontab -l` probe\n- preserve explicit selection through `--only core/doctor/legacy-whatsapp-crontab` and `--all`\n- add selection coverage proving default lint skips the probe while selected lint reports the warning\n\n## Public surface\n- No public SDK/plugin/config contract changes.\n- Default `doctor --lint` changes only by skipping this live crontab probe; `--all` and `--only` still include it.\n\n## PR surface\n- 2 files changed, +55/-0.\n\n## Validation\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.test.ts` (60 tests)\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/flows/doctor-core-checks.test.ts` (18 tests)\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check src/flows/doctor-core-checks.ts src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.test.ts`\n- `pnpm exec oxlint src/flows/doctor-core-checks.ts src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/plugin-sdk-surface-report.mjs --check`\n- `git diff --check`\n\n## Not tested\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/commands/doctor/cron/index.test.ts` still has a Windows permission-mode assertion failure in `falls back to copy+unlink when renaming the legacy cron store fails with EXDEV` (`archiveStat.mode & 0o777` returned `0o666` instead of `0o640`). This PR does not touch cron storage implementation; focused lint-selection and core-check tests passed.",
